# Fixed u64 workload → RC04 receipt bridge

Private app-owned composition. No process owner, Store ledger transition, desired verdict input, generic recipe registry or admission authority. Source snapshots are retained in `evidence/inputs.json`. Implementation is in `src/app/u64_receipt.rs` and its three focused subordinate files.

## Public composition order

1. `publish_expectation(&mut Evidence, &protected_snapshot, &Recipe, deadline)` publishes the exact frozen oracle, exact fixed public wrapper, three common-origin cutoffs, black-box assumptions and `ExpectationV1`. Returned `FrozenExpectation` exposes `reference`, `specification`, `wrapper`, and `recipe`. It grants no approval.
2. An independent reviewer examines that exact expectation graph and publishes `ReviewV1` with source-grounded provenance. Required action is `case_design_review`, disposition accepted, exact expectation SHA, no material open/accepted-residual finding or unsettled material obligation. An unrelated bootstrap review cannot substitute.
3. The trusted front end prepares one selected mandatory case, all source/support subjects, actual host/tool observations, and exact patch. It calls `prepare(&Evidence, Preparation)` before dispatch. The result `Frozen` owns clones of `Prepared`, source/protected snapshots and tool pins; no self-referential borrows or post-run reconstruction. `Frozen::prepared()` provides a shared reference for later import.
4. Existing workload/process/namespace/aggregate owners execute and settle. The app retains the actual `Run` and aggregate cleanup observations.
5. `observe(&Frozen, &Run)` invokes the trusted in-process `FrozenOracle` against retained driver stdout and stamps its actual completion. It can run after aggregate cleanup. `OracleObservation` is opaque and binds stdout SHA and sampled terminal report end. No external checker exit0 is invented.
6. `finalize(&mut Evidence, &Frozen, &Run, &OracleObservation, Clock, &Cleanup, deadline)` derives `decision::Decision`, publishes exact typed graph via Publisher, and returns `Collected { receipt, decision, decision_inputs, oracle_observation }`. The caller transfers the exact closure through `receipt_import` before Store verification. No task transition occurs here.

